ts the reply from inst.vbal, SendMsg calls the captured Marshal, and a fresh object decodes the resulting bytes as in replicaListener. The fixed codec contains no VBallot write or assignment. The applicable local responsibility is preservation of the prior value ballot needed by handlePrepareReply at lines 1239-1246; this conclusion does not require a chosen quorum. The reduced initialization omits runtime scheduling and capacity, neither of which changes this synchronous serializer endpoint.\",\n        \"answers\": {},\n        \"knowledge\": [],\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"The zero-ballot control retains its original value; the problem is masked when the producer value ballot equals the fresh object default.\",\n          \"Other sampled fields, including current ballot, status, commands, sequence and dependencies, are retained in these cases.\"\n        ],\n        \"limitations\": [\n          \"No recovery consumer selection, conflicting decision, FSM effect or client completion was executed in this probe.\",\n          \"The recovery invocation at an empty peer is supplied; no timeout-triggered distributed history is claimed.\"\n        ],\n        \"joint_history\": \"\",\n        \"failure_attribution\": null,\n        \"report_title\": null,\n        \"report_answer\": null,\n        \"operation_id\": \"d02596af8410432ea84a76fab33b8b79\"\n      },\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"3b68c48182e94ac9a967a16fbe03ce7b-question-0\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"3b68c48182e94ac9a967a16fbe03ce7b-question-1\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"Does successful handleAccept retain enough phase status for a later recovery to distinguish accepted state from preaccepted or empty state?\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"handleAccept updates ballots and attributes but appears not to set Status to ACCEPTED; prepare may consequently report a weaker phase.\